---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Pic from '../components/Pic.astro';
import ChestDiagram from '../components/ChestDiagram.astro';
import SizeCompare from '../components/SizeCompare.astro';
import WorkBand from '../components/WorkBand.astro';
import LabLink from '../components/LabLink.astro';
import { LAB } from '../config';
---
<Base title="The device" description="A small stiff core with six magnetic sensors, two soft ECG wings, and its place on the breastbone.">

<section class="phero" aria-labelledby="h-page">
  <div class="wrap phero-in">
    <div class="phero-text">
      <p class="chip">The device</p>
      <h1 id="h-page" class="display display-m">One piece.<span class="teal">Six sensors.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">A small stiff core with two soft wings. It sits on the breastbone and records two signals from the same heartbeat.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <LabLink href={LAB.option1}>The device in the research tools</LabLink>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="phero-art">
      <Pic name="device-detail" class="render fade-edges" eager sizes="(max-width: 900px) 92vw, 56vw" alt="Close view of the white core with its teal ring and a woven wing ending in a round electrode pad." />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-tight" aria-label="Key dimensions">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="specs" data-r>
      <div class="spec"><b>60<small>x 32 x 9 mm</small></b><span>The core. Small and stiff on purpose.</span></div>
      <div class="spec"><b>6</b><span>Magnetic sensors, wound from fine wire, standing in the core.</span></div>
      <div class="spec"><b>2</b><span>Soft wings that carry the ECG electrodes.</span></div>
      <div class="spec"><b>40<small>mAh</small></b><span>The battery is inside the core. One piece, no pod, no tail.</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-mist" aria-labelledby="h-inside">
  <div class="wrap split split-wide-media">
    <div class="split-text" data-r>
      <p class="chip">Inside</p>
      <h2 id="h-inside" class="h2">Everything in<span class="teal">the core.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">Six wire sensors read the heart. A seventh reads the room, so that what the room adds can be taken out.</p>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>Six magnetic sensors in a small stiff core</li>
        <li>One three-axis reference sensor, fitted against each heart sensor</li>
        <li>A flat coil for the self-test</li>
        <li>Battery and electronics in the same shell</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="split-media frame frame-multiply" data-r>
      <Pic name="device-open" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 92vw, 54vw" alt="The device opened into layers: lid, flexible sheet with the wings, a flat coil, the sensor board with upright wire sensors, the shell and a soft pad." />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="h-small">
  <div class="wrap split split-wide-text">
    <div class="split-media" data-r>
      <div class="panel panel-wide"><SizeCompare /></div>
    </div>
    <div class="split-text" data-r>
      <p class="chip">Small on purpose</p>
      <h2 id="h-small" class="h2">Closer to<span class="teal">the chest.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">A stiff plate cannot follow a curved chest. A small one barely has to.</p>
      <p>On 42 scanned chests, the largest gap under a bank-card-sized plate was 9.50 mm. Under the small core it was 4.45 mm. Closer to the chest is closer to the heart.</p>
      <p><a class="textlink" href="/evidence/">See the evidence</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-tint" aria-labelledby="h-ecg">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split-text" data-r>
      <p class="chip">Its own ECG</p>
      <h2 id="h-ecg" class="h2">Two soft wings.<span class="teal">Two signals.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">The wings carry the ECG electrodes. The ECG marks each beat, and the magnetic beats are averaged on that mark.</p>
      <p class="pull">An ECG does not determine the magnetic field. That is the reason to record both.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="split-media frame frame-white frame-flush" data-r>
      <Pic name="device-wing" alt="A soft white woven wing joining the core beside its teal ring." />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="h-worn">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="split split-wide-text">
      <div class="split-media frame frame-flush" data-r>
        <ChestDiagram variant="body" alt="The front of a chest outlined from a scan: skin, breastbone, ribs and the heart behind them, with the device on the lower breastbone and its two wings reaching to each side." />
      </div>
      <div class="split-text" data-r>
        <p class="chip">Where it is worn</p>
        <h2 id="h-worn" class="h2">On the breastbone.<span class="teal">A zone, not a point.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">Slide a finger down the middle of your chest until the bone stops. The device is centred just above that.</p>
        <div class="stats">
          <div class="stat"><b>3<small>cm</small></b><span>above where the bone stops</span></div>
          <div class="stat stat-dim"><b>1<small>cm</small></b><span>to the right costs 1.4 times the beats in the virtual trial</span></div>
        </div>
        <p>In the virtual trial the place is forgiving toward the wearer's left, and a little up or down. On the scans, the middle gap under the core at this place is about 5 mm.</p>
        <p><a class="textlink" href="/reading/">How a reading goes</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-mist" aria-labelledby="h-wear">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split-text" data-r>
      <p class="chip">Ways to wear it</p>
      <h2 id="h-wear" class="h2">Three carriers.<span class="teal">One core.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">Three ways to wear the same core.</p>
      <ol class="rows">
        <li><span class="ring r1">1</span><div><h3>Chest strap</h3><p>An elastic strap with a cradle that presses the core to the skin. The lead carrier of the three.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="ring r1">2</span><div><h3>Stick-on carrier</h3><p>A skin-safe carrier holds the core and the wings. The core clips out and is kept.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="ring r1">3</span><div><h3>Built into a garment</h3><p>The core docks in a pocket at the breastbone, with nothing of steel near it.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="split-media frame frame-flush" data-r>
      <Pic name="garment-flat" alt="A soft garment laid flat with a pocket at the breastbone and two fabric electrodes, and the device beside it." />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="h-case">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split-text" data-r>
      <p class="chip">Between readings</p>
      <h2 id="h-case" class="h2">Kept in<span class="teal">its case.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">Between readings the device lives in its charging case. No magnets and no wireless charging, by design.</p>
      <p>One piece, and the case that charges it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="split-media frame frame-multiply" data-r>
      <Pic name="case" alt="A navy charging case, open, with a moulded white tray and a row of gold charging contacts." />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<WorkBand />
</Base>
